{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"arachnidan-esophageal-honeybee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"On the Gerrit Verified gate, tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py::test_matching_guard_is_accepted intermittently crashes its pytest-xdist worker ('worker gwN crashed'; '[gwN] node down: Not properly terminated'), failing the whole matrix job and producing a spurious Verified-1. Hard worker-process death (not an assertion), lands on a RANDOM matrix job per run (~1 of 4), timing/platform-dependent. Observed 4+ consecutive times 2026-08-08 blocking change 1545 (ticket ad16), whose diff is markdown/comment-only and cannot touch opcert_service. The opcert app lifespan cancels+awaits its worker tasks correctly, so the crash likely originates in the TestClient lifespan/anyio portal or an asyncio.to_thread interaction under xdist load; reproduction is CI-only. Impact: any change can be spuriously Verified-1'd, forcing ~24min rechecks. Fix: harden the opcert TestClient fixture/app teardown against the xdist worker crash (or quarantine-serialize this test), then confirm consecutive green runs.","id":"fade-ea90-7564-4715","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Flaky CI: pytest-xdist worker crash on test_opcert_service_app::test_matching_guard_is_accepted"},"env_id":"4d084713-8164-4b68-9afe-601bbda46966","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786191971481095001,"uuid":"80cbbf71-9959-4820-9868-4c3c42c3d697"}